== 4.11 Chapter 4 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The rate of a chemical reaction is defined as the change in],
  [temperature per unit time],
  [mass per unit time],
  [concentration of a reactant or product per unit time],
  [volume per unit time]
)

#mcq(2, [Which unit is appropriate for the rate of a reaction?],
  [mol dm⁻³],
  [dm³ s⁻¹],
  [mol s⁻¹],
  [mol dm⁻³ s⁻¹]
)

#mcq(3, [According to collision theory, a reaction occurs when particles collide with],
  [high mass],
  [any energy],
  [a catalyst],
  [sufficient energy and the correct orientation]
)

#mcq(4, [Increasing the temperature of a reaction increases the rate because],
  [the concentration rises],
  [the particles get larger],
  [the activation energy falls],
  [more particles have energy greater than the activation energy]
)

#mcq(5, [Which change does NOT increase the rate of a reaction between a solid and an acid?],
  [increasing the acid concentration],
  [cooling the acid],
  [stirring the mixture],
  [powdering the solid]
)

#mcq(6, [A catalyst increases the rate of reaction by],
  [changing ΔH],
  [increasing the concentration],
  [providing an alternative path of lower activation energy],
  [increasing the temperature]
)

#mcq(7, [Which statement about a catalyst is correct?],
  [it is not used up, though it may change form],
  [it changes the enthalpy change],
  [it only works for exothermic reactions],
  [it is used up in the reaction]
)

#mcq(8, [In a reaction between marble chips and dilute hydrochloric acid, the rate can be followed by measuring],
  [the colour change only],
  [the pH only],
  [the mass of the acid],
  [the volume of carbon dioxide given off with time]
)

#mcq(9, [The rate of the reaction Mg + 2HCl → MgCl₂ + H₂ is fastest],
  [without stirring],
  [with cold dilute acid],
  [with magnesium powder],
  [with a large ribbon of magnesium]
)

#mcq(10, [Which graph shape shows a reaction slowing down as it proceeds?],
  [a curve that becomes less steep],
  [a rising straight line],
  [a horizontal line],
  [a line going down]
)

#mcq(11, [Rate of reaction is greatest],
  [at the end],
  [at any time equally],
  [at the beginning when concentrations are highest],
  [in the middle]
)

#mcq(12, [Which factor will increase the rate of a gaseous reaction?],
  [lowering the pressure],
  [cooling the gases],
  [using a larger vessel],
  [increasing the pressure]
)

#mcq(13, [A reaction between two solutions is fastest when they are],
  [concentrated and cold],
  [concentrated and warm],
  [dilute and cold],
  [dilute and warm]
)

#mcq(14, [When zinc granules react with excess dilute acid, the total volume of hydrogen produced depends on],
  [the amount of zinc used],
  [the temperature only],
  [the rate of stirring],
  [the surface area of the zinc]
)

#mcq(15, [Which pair of changes both increase the rate?],
  [increase in surface area and decrease in temperature],
  [decrease in concentration and increase in temperature],
  [increase in surface area and increase in temperature],
  [cooling and dilution]
)

#mcq(16, [A reaction has been catalysed by manganese(IV) oxide in the decomposition of hydrogen peroxide. At the end, the MnO₂],
  [has dissolved],
  [is found unchanged in mass],
  [has reacted to give oxygen],
  [has been used up]
)

#mcq(17, [A catalyst that is in the same phase as the reactants is called],
  [poisoned],
  [promoted],
  [heterogeneous],
  [homogeneous]
)

#mcq(18, [Enzymes are biological catalysts that are],
  [inorganic and heat stable],
  [always solid],
  [metals],
  [protein and specific in action]
)

#mcq(19, [Which observation suggests a reaction is complete?],
  [the temperature falls],
  [the mixture stops changing and the limiting reactant is used up],
  [the colour deepens],
  [bubbles increase in number]
)

#mcq(20, [The rate constant is affected by],
  [the volume of the vessel],
  [the concentration of reactants],
  [the time taken],
  [temperature]
)

#mcq(21, [In the reaction A + B → C, doubling the concentration of A doubles the rate. This suggests the reaction is],
  [first order in A],
  [second order overall],
  [second order in A],
  [zero order in A]
)

#mcq(22, [If doubling the concentration of both A and B increases the rate fourfold when the order in B is first, the order in A is],
  [first],
  [third],
  [second],
  [zero]
)

#mcq(23, [Which one of these is a heterogeneous catalyst?],
  [iron in the Haber process],
  [an enzyme in solution],
  [chlorine atoms in the ozone layer],
  [H⁺(aq) in esterification]
)

#mcq(24, [A catalyst poison is a substance that],
  [changes the products],
  [increases the rate],
  [destroys the catalyst's activity],
  [acts as a reactant]
)

#mcq(25, [Which of the following would produce the steepest initial rate curve for Mg + acid?],
  [1 g of large chips in 1.0 M acid],
  [1 g of powder in 1.0 M acid],
  [1 g of large chips in 0.5 M acid],
  [1 g of powder in 0.5 M acid]
)

#mcq(26, [In a plot of volume of gas against time, the final plateau shows],
  [the rate is increasing],
  [the reaction has ended],
  [the reaction is stopped by the catalyst],
  [the temperature has risen]
)

#mcq(27, [In the Maxwell–Boltzmann distribution, raising the temperature],
  [moves the peak to lower energy and reduces the tail],
  [lowers the curve only],
  [has no effect],
  [shifts the curve to the right and increases the area beyond E_a]
)

#mcq(28, [Which part of the Maxwell–Boltzmann curve lies above the activation energy for a typical reaction at room temperature?],
  [a very small fraction],
  [about half],
  [all of it],
  [none]
)

#mcq(29, [Rate of reaction can also be expressed as the rate of],
  [change of mass only],
  [change of pressure only],
  [change of colour],
  [disappearance of a reactant or appearance of a product]
)

#mcq(30, [Which statement is true of a reaction at equilibrium that is still proceeding rapidly?],
  [the forward and reverse rates are equal and nonzero],
  [the reverse rate is zero],
  [the forward rate is zero],
  [concentrations are changing]
)

#mcq(31, [Which would least affect the rate of reaction of marble chips with acid?],
  [using finer chips],
  [adding more acid],
  [raising the temperature],
  [placing the vessel under stronger light]
)

#mcq(32, [The collision frequency between gas molecules rises when],
  [the volume is decreased],
  [the temperature falls],
  [the pressure falls],
  [the volume is increased]
)

#mcq(33, [A reaction with a very high activation energy at room temperature is],
  [instantaneous],
  [slow until heated],
  [unaffected by temperature],
  [always explosive]
)

#mcq(34, [Light-catalysed reactions such as the chlorination of methane are examples of],
  [catalytic poisoning],
  [photochemical activation],
  [thermal activation],
  [electrochemical activation]
)

#mcq(35, [Which change would slow the reaction between sodium thiosulphate and acid?],
  [using a finer solid],
  [warming the mixture],
  [diluting with water],
  [using more concentrated acid]
)

#mcq(36, [A student records the time for a cross to disappear under a cloudy solution. As the time increases, the rate],
  [decreases],
  [increases],
  [becomes zero],
  [stays the same]
)

#mcq(37, [Which statement about the effect of a catalyst on the position of equilibrium is correct?],
  [it has no effect on the position],
  [it shifts it to the right],
  [it destroys the products],
  [it shifts it to the left]
)

#mcq(38, [For the reaction CaCO₃ + 2HCl → CaCl₂ + H₂O + CO₂, the rate can be followed by the loss in mass because],
  [carbon dioxide escapes as a gas],
  [calcium chloride is a gas],
  [water evaporates],
  [the acid is volatile]
)

#mcq(39, [Reaction rate usually increases with temperature roughly],
  [not changing],
  [doubling for every 10 K rise],
  [falling by half for every 10 K rise],
  [doubling for every 100 K rise]
)

#mcq(40, [Which of these reactions is fastest at room temperature?],
  [decay of a radioactive element],
  [burning of coal],
  [iron rusting],
  [precipitation of silver chloride on mixing solutions]
)

